 swing of the game. Black's lead went from +8.4 to -7.8. The engine's first choice here was E8, and the 12k never got back in front."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "Opus 5.5 found E8, the engine's first choice, and lost -0.1 points with it. From here every move on both sides cost almost nothing, and the lead held at about -7.8 for White to the final pass."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills each group on a pasted board and prints its stones and liberties, flagging groups with two or fewer. count.py counts stones and enclosed empty regions after the player marks stones as dead, then adds komi. Both only analyse the position given, and neither generates, scores or ranks candidate moves or plays out any continuation.", "stop": false}}